-- title:
--   Invariant element avoiding every valuation ring over another supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A, M')$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, an inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A,M')$, a distinguished $s \in W$, an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, a prime $\ell'$, an intermediate field $K_\ell$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$ carrying an algebra and scalar-tower structure over $A \cap k_0 = A.\mathrm{comap}$, a nonzero $j_\ell \in K_\ell$, a subalgebra $B_t$ and a valuation subring $W_t$ of $K_\ell$ with $B_t \subseteq W_t$, together with the further data $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$, $\ell$, $\zeta_0$, $\varpi_t$, $K_b$, $A_b$ (the valuation subring of $K_b$ induced by $A$), $\varpi_b$, $\xi \in k_0$, $\varpi_t'$, an ideal $y$ of the $j$-finite chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}_{A\cap k_0}(K_\ell, j_\ell)$, $n$, $\gamma_0 \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, a $k_0$-automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K_\ell$, $m$, an element $\zeta_c$ of the adic completion of $A \cap k_0$ at its maximal ideal, the membership $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell') \in K_\ell$, $a_0 \in A\cap k_0$ and a finite set $\mathrm{ends}$ of subrings of $K_\ell$, all of which enter as the arguments of a term $\mathcal F$ of the rigid-descent hypothesis structure $\mathrm{RigidDescentHyps}$ for exactly these arguments (summarised here). Let $G$ be the subgroup of $k_0$-automorphisms of $K_\ell$ generated by those $\tau$ for which some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ satisfies $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_\ell\,\tau$, that is, $\tau$ realises on $q$-expansions the action of $\gamma$ on ratios of integral modular forms of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ under any embedding sending $\xi$ to $e^{2\pi i/(q\ell')}$; let $K_0$ be the fixed field of $G$, let $B_0$ consist of the $G$-invariant elements of $B_t$, and let $W_0'$ be the valuation subring of $K_0$ obtained by intersecting with $W_t$. The conclusion is: for every $s' \in W$ with $s' \ne s$ there is $b \in K_0$ whose image in $K_\ell$ lies in $B_0$ and which lies in no valuation subring $V$ of $K_0$ with the following two properties: first, an element of $k_0$ lies in $A$ if and only if its image in $K_0$ lies in $V$; second, for every $g \in \mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}(jq) \ge 0$ also $P.\mathrm{ord}(g) \ge 0$, and such that $R_0$'s residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s'$, the element $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ of $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,g$, whenever it lies in $K_\ell$, lies in $K_0$ and in $V$, and for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ equals the value at $s'$ of $R_0$'s residue of $g$, the difference of that element and $c$ lies in $V$ and in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   This is the separation step, at the level of the $G$-fixed field $K_0$, which rules out that a valuation ring of $K_0$ normalised by the $q$-expansion conditions at a supersingular place $s' \ne s$ can contain all of the invariant chart algebra $B_0$: one invariant element witnesses the exclusion. It feeds the assembly of the supersingular discrete valuation ring together with its affine chart, poles, moduli-Hasse data and nodes in the rigid-descent construction.
